       "{'id': 'chatcmpl-BgdYOrjIDHS1Dffc58MsG5gftKWrY',\n",
       " 'choices': [{'finish_reason': 'stop',\n",
       "   'index': 0,\n",
       "   'logprobs': None,\n",
       "   'message': {'content': '{\"courses\":[\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 002\",\"name\":\"Introduction to Mechanical Engineering\",\"description\":\"An introduction to the field of mechanical engineering. Topics include the mechanical engineering profession; machine components; forces in structures and fluids; materials and stresses; thermal and energy systems; machine motion; and machine design.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 003\",\"name\":\"How Things Work: the Principles Behind Technology\",\"description\":\"Introduces the basic physical principles of engineering systems from everyday life such as automobiles, computers, and household appliances. Topics include conservation laws and the physics and chemistry of engineering systems. Does not confer credit towards a degree in the Bourns College of Engineering.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 004\",\"name\":\"Energy and the Environment\",\"description\":\"Covers energy conservation, energy sources, market dynamics, and climate change. Addresses cultural, political, and social trends and their impact on the ecosystem. Discusses renewable and non-renewable energy sources. Technical background not required.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 005\",\"name\":\"The Science of Mythbusting\",\"description\":\"Introduces the scientific method for non-science majors. Explores the application of scientific concepts to test the validity of myths and events from news stories, movies, and other popular media. Provides critical reasoning skills to interpret product claims, critique Web information, and understand new technologies.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 009\",\"name\":\"Engineering Graphics and Design\",\"description\":\"Covers graphical concepts and projective geometry relating to spatial visualization and communication in design. Includes technical sketching, computer-aided design with solid modeling, geometric dimensioning and tolerancing, and an introduction to the engineering design process.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 010\",\"name\":\"Statics\",\"description\":\"Covers equilibrium of coplanar force systems; analysis of frames and trusses; non-coplanar force systems; friction; and distributed loads.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 018A\",\"name\":\"Introduction to Engineering Computation\",\"description\":\"Introduces the use of MATLAB in engineering computation. Covers scripts and functions, programming, input/output, two- and three-dimensional graphics, and elementary numerical analysis.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 018B\",\"name\":\"Introduction to Computational Modeling in Mechanical Engineering\",\"description\":\"Introduces concepts of computational modeling in mechanical engineering. Topics include formulation of models using vector analysis, linear algebra, differential and integral calculus, and both analytical and numerical solution techniques.\",\"level\":\"lower\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 100A\",\"name\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"description\":\"Introduces basic concepts and applications of thermodynamics relevant to mechanical engineering. Topics include work and energy, the first law, properties of pure substances, control volume analysis, Carnot cycle, refrigeration cycles, the second law, entropy, and reversible versus irreversible processes.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 100B\",\"name\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"description\":\"Continuation of ME 100A. Topics include entropy production, cycle analysis, vapor and gas power systems, refrigeration and heat pump systems, equations of state, property relations, ideal gas mixtures, psychrometrics, multicomponent systems, combustion, and reacting mixtures.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 103\",\"name\":\"Dynamics\",\"description\":\"Covers kinematics and kinetics of particles and rigid bodies using vector methods. Topics include Newton’s laws, work-energy, impulse-momentum, and analysis of systems of particles and rigid bodies.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 110\",\"name\":\"Mechanics of Materials\",\"description\":\"Studies deformable bodies under axial, torsional, shear, and bending loads; combined stresses; and applications to structural design.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 113\",\"name\":\"Fluid Mechanics\",\"description\":\"Introduces fluid mechanics principles. Topics include viscosity, fluid statics, Bernoulli and energy equations, control-volume analysis, differential equations of motion, turbulent pipe flow, and external flow lift and drag.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 114\",\"name\":\"Introduction to Materials Science and Engineering\",\"description\":\"Covers classification of materials, atomic and crystal structure, defects, diffusion, mechanical properties, strengthening, fracture and fatigue, phase diagrams, ceramics, polymers, and composites.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 116A\",\"name\":\"Heat Transfer\",\"description\":\"Introduces steady and transient conduction, fins, two-dimensional conduction, forced and natural convection, radiation heat transfer, heat exchangers, and basics of mass transfer.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 116B\",\"name\":\"Heat Transfer\",\"description\":\"Covers analytical and numerical methods in heat transfer and fluid mechanics, including conduction, convection, radiation, boiling, condensation, phase change, mass transfer, multimode heat transfer, and thermal simulation.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 117\",\"name\":\"Combustion and Energy Systems\",\"description\":\"Discusses premixed and diffusion flames, fuel-air thermochemistry, engine cycle analysis, combustion-driven engine design and operation, fluid mechanics of engine components, pollutant formation, and gas turbines.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 118\",\"name\":\"Mechanical Engineering Modeling and Analysis\",\"description\":\"Introduces data analysis and numerical modeling in MATLAB. Topics include statistics, sampling, curve fitting, interpolation, numerical differentiation/integration, and solving ordinary differential equations, culminating in a system modeling project.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 120\",\"name\":\"Linear Systems and Controls\",\"description\":\"Introduces modeling and analysis of dynamic systems across mechanical, thermal, electrical, and fluid domains. Covers state equations, equilibrium, linearization, stability, and time- and frequency-domain analysis.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 121\",\"name\":\"Feedback Control\",\"description\":\"Covers analysis and design of feedback control systems using classical methods. Topics include block diagrams, time- and frequency-domain design, stability, root locus, Bode plots, and introductory state-space analysis.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 122\",\"name\":\"Vibrations\",\"description\":\"Studies free and forced vibration of single and multiple degree-of-freedom systems, damping, resonance, normal modes, coupling, and energy methods.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 130\",\"name\":\"Kinematic and Dynamic Analysis of Mechanisms\",\"description\":\"Explores kinematic analysis of planar mechanisms such as linkages, cams, and gear trains and introduces multibody dynamics concepts.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 131\",\"name\":\"Design of Mechanisms\",\"description\":\"Focuses on the design of planar, spherical, and spatial mechanisms using graphical and analytical methods and requires a computer-aided design project.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 133\",\"name\":\"Introduction to Mechatronics\",\"description\":\"Introduces hardware, software, sensors, actuators, system modeling, and control for mechatronic systems. Topics include data acquisition, electronics, signal processing, PLCs, and microcontroller programming with MATLAB/Simulink.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 134\",\"name\":\"Microstructural Transformations in Materials\",\"description\":\"Studies thermodynamics and kinetics governing liquid-solid and solid-solid microstructural transformations that control the properties of crystalline materials. Cross-listed with MSE 134.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 135\",\"name\":\"Transport Phenomena\",\"description\":\"Integrates thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, and heat transfer to cover psychrometry, combustion, compressible flow, turbomachinery, and combined momentum, heat, and mass transport.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 136\",\"name\":\"Environmental Impacts of Energy Production and Conversion\",\"description\":\"Applies thermodynamics, heat transfer, and fluid mechanics to evaluate environmental impacts of energy use. Topics include fossil-fuel pollution, turbulent pollutant transport, and design principles for pollution control equipment.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 137\",\"name\":\"Environmental Fluid Mechanics\",\"description\":\"Applies fluid mechanics to atmospheric and oceanic flows. Topics include hydrostatic and geostrophic balance, Coriolis effects, boundary layers, turbulence, and tracer and heat transport.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 138\",\"name\":\"Transport Phenomena in Living Systems\",\"description\":\"Introduces conservation laws of mass, momentum, and energy applied to modeling complex biological systems, highlighting prediction and explanation of life processes.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 140\",\"name\":\"Ship Theory\",\"description\":\"Covers hull form, static and dynamic stability, ship response to waves, grounding, flooding, 3-D numerical integration, and modeling curved surfaces for naval applications.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 144\",\"name\":\"Introduction to Robotics\",\"description\":\"Surveys robot components, kinematics, dynamics, control strategies, sensors, vision, and programming. Includes laboratory projects on robot arms, vision, and mobile robots. Cross-listed with EE 144.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 145\",\"name\":\"Robotic Planning and Kinematics\",\"description\":\"Covers motion planning and kinematics with emphasis on geometric reasoning and computation. Topics include configuration spaces, sampling methods, planning algorithms, and reference-frame kinematics. Cross-listed with EE 145.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 153\",\"name\":\"Finite Element Methods\",\"description\":\"Introduces weak form formulation, Galerkin method, mesh generation, data visualization, and programming of finite element codes for engineering applications.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 156\",\"name\":\"Mechanical Behavior of Materials\",\"description\":\"Covers experimental techniques and theory for mechanical behavior of metals, ceramics, polymers, composites, and electronic materials, including deformation mechanisms, failure modes, and materials selection.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 170A\",\"name\":\"Experimental Techniques\",\"description\":\"Introduces measurement and control principles, experiment design, dimensional and error analysis, data acquisition, filtering, statistical analysis, and technical reporting.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 170B\",\"name\":\"Experimental Techniques\",\"description\":\"Provides advanced, project-oriented laboratory experiments to verify fluid, thermal, structural, thermodynamic, and electromechanical theories through measurement and analysis.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 174\",\"name\":\"Machine Design\",\"description\":\"Introduces strength-based design fundamentals including stiffness, deflection, static failure, and fatigue failure criteria.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 175A\",\"name\":\"Professional Topics in Engineering\",\"description\":\"Covers technical communication, teamwork, project management, engineering economics, professional ethics, and CAD for senior-level mechanical engineers.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 175B\",\"name\":\"Mechanical Engineering Design\",\"description\":\"Guides students through problem definition, concept generation, and detailed design, emphasizing safety, reliability, manufacturing, and assembly considerations.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 175C\",\"name\":\"Mechanical Engineering Design\",\"description\":\"Students prototype, test, and evaluate a design initiated in ME 175B, studying prototyping techniques, design verification, and special design topics.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 175D\",\"name\":\"Technological Entrepreneurship\",\"description\":\"Introduces business and management concepts for commercializing technology, including market analysis, strategy, finance, IP, ethics, and communication.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 176\",\"name\":\"Sustainable Product Design\",\"description\":\"Covers life-cycle design, reliability, recyclability, materials selection, and manufacturing for sustainable products, with a redesign project to reduce environmental impact.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 180\",\"name\":\"Optics and Lasers in Engineering\",\"description\":\"Focuses on optics and laser principles, interferometry, diffraction, laser-material interactions, and applications such as microscopy, spectroscopy, deformation analysis, and materials processing.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 190\",\"name\":\"Special Studies\",\"description\":\"Individual study under faculty supervision to meet special curricular needs; culminates in a written report. Repeatable for credit.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 197\",\"name\":\"Research for Undergraduates\",\"description\":\"Directed undergraduate research in mechanical engineering culminating in a technical report. Repeatable for credit.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 198\",\"name\":\"R’course: Variable Topics\",\"description\":\"Student-facilitated course fostering leadership and curricular innovation; topics vary and emphasize experiential education. Repeatable as topics change.\",\"level\":\"upper\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 200\",\"name\":\"Methods of Engineering Analysis\",\"description\":\"Covers linear algebra, vector spaces, eigenvalue problems, complex analysis, integral transforms, and analytical methods for differential equations in engineering applications.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 201\",\"name\":\"Computational Methods in Engineering\",\"description\":\"Explores numerical methods for nonlinear equations, linear systems, interpolation, integration, data statistics, model fitting, FFT, and differential equation solutions.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 202\",\"name\":\"Spectral Computational Methods\",\"description\":\"Covers Fourier analysis, eigenfunction expansions, spectral/Galerkin/tau/collocation methods, aliasing, stability, and applications to compressible and incompressible flows and reacting systems.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 203\",\"name\":\"Design and Analysis of Engineering Experiments\",\"description\":\"Introduces experimental design, statistical tools, time and frequency-domain data analysis, machine learning, pattern recognition, and computational research tools.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 210\",\"name\":\"Sustainable Product Design\",\"description\":\"Graduate-level treatment of sustainable product design including life-cycle analysis, reliability, materials selection, and manufacturing, with an environmental impact redesign project.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 220\",\"name\":\"Optimal Control and Estimation\",\"description\":\"Covers discrete-time optimal control, Riccati equations, optimal tracking, receding-horizon control, Kalman filtering, EKF, and UKF for linear systems. Cross-listed with EE 233.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 222\",\"name\":\"Advanced Robotics\",\"description\":\"Studies robot navigation, sensor modeling, data processing, localization, SLAM, image-based motion estimation, mapping, and motion planning. Cross-listed with EE 245.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 223\",\"name\":\"Secure and Reliable Control Systems\",\"description\":\"Introduces fault-tolerant and secure control, attack detectability, fault detection, analytical redundancy, unknown-input observers, statistical methods, and fault-tolerant control design.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 230\",\"name\":\"Computer-Aided Engineering Design\",\"description\":\"Covers interactive graphics, 3-D curve and surface representations, Bézier parameterization, optimization, and applications to CAD and mechanical system simulation.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 231\",\"name\":\"Pen-Based Computing\",\"description\":\"Explores ink segmentation, sketch parsing, shape recognition, context reasoning, error correction, and practical system issues for pen-based interfaces. Cross-listed with CS 233.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 232\",\"name\":\"Computational Design Tools\",\"description\":\"Introduces geometric modeling, numerical optimization, and AI techniques for engineering design, with programming projects combining symbolic and numerical methods.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 233\",\"name\":\"Artificial Intelligence for Design\",\"description\":\"Applies AI—search, knowledge-based systems, machine learning, qualitative reasoning—to automate engineering design, covering theory and practical issues.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 235\",\"name\":\"Linear System Theory\",\"description\":\"Reviews linear algebra and presents state-space modeling, controllability, observability, realizations, and design via state feedback, pole placement, and observers. Cross-listed with EE 235.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 236\",\"name\":\"State and Parameter Estimation Theory\",\"description\":\"Covers statistical estimation, Fisher information, CRLB, least squares, ML, MAP estimators, Wiener and Kalman filtering, with applications in navigation and signal processing. Cross-listed with EE 236.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 237\",\"name\":\"Nonlinear Systems and Control\",\"description\":\"Studies nonlinear differential equations, phase portraits, limit cycles, describing functions, Lyapunov stability, absolute stability criteria, averaging, and feedback linearization. Cross-listed with EE 237.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 238\",\"name\":\"Linear Multivariable Control\",\"description\":\"Analyzes multivariable feedback systems, robustness, Q-parameterization, H-infinity design, and structured singular value methods. Cross-listed with EE 238.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 239\",\"name\":\"Optimal Control\",\"description\":\"Presents stochastic optimal control, optimization principles, LQG control, certainty equivalence, Pontryagin minimum principle, HJB equation, and algebraic Riccati equation. Cross-listed with EE 239.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 240A\",\"name\":\"Fundamentals of Fluid Mechanics\",\"description\":\"Introduces equations of motion, stress tensor, Navier-Stokes equations, boundary conditions, exact viscous solutions, vorticity dynamics, and boundary layers.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 240B\",\"name\":\"Fundamentals of Fluid Mechanics\",\"description\":\"Covers inviscid flow, Euler and Bernoulli equations, potential flow, wing theory, flow stability, and turbulence introduction.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 241A\",\"name\":\"Fundamentals of Heat and Mass Transfer\",\"description\":\"Derives governing equations for conduction, convection, radiation, and species transport, emphasizing problem formulation and analytical/numerical solutions.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 241B\",\"name\":\"Transport Through Porous Media\",\"description\":\"Examines flow, heat, and mass transfer mechanisms in multiphase porous media using current theoretical models.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 241C\",\"name\":\"Electronic Cooling and Thermal Issues in Microelectronics\",\"description\":\"Discusses thermal challenges in electronics, passive/active/hybrid cooling, computational modeling, and advanced techniques such as phase-change and heat pipes.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 242\",\"name\":\"Turbulence in Fluids\",\"description\":\"Applies conservation laws to turbulent flows, covering tensor notation, statistical and spectral analysis, and closure techniques for complex turbulence modeling.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 243\",\"name\":\"Advanced Mechanical Engineering Thermodynamics\",\"description\":\"Explores statistical foundations of thermodynamics, origins of entropy and temperature, phase and chemical equilibria, fluctuations, and nanoscale thermodynamics.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 244\",\"name\":\"Nanoscale Heat Transfer and Energy Conversion\",\"description\":\"Studies energy transport at nanoscale involving electrons, phonons, photons, size effects, carrier coupling, and Boltzmann transport modeling.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 245\",\"name\":\"Radiative Heat Transfer\",\"description\":\"Provides an in-depth study of radiative heat transfer phenomena, extending undergraduate radiation topics to advanced analytical and numerical methods.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 246\",\"name\":\"Computational Fluid Dynamics with Applications\",\"description\":\"Introduces finite difference, finite volume, finite element, and spectral methods for reacting/non-reacting flows, with stability and convergence analysis and CFD software projects.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 248\",\"name\":\"Internal Combustion Engines\",\"description\":\"Covers engine types, design parameters, fuel-air thermochemistry, cycles, spark/compression ignition, performance, and emissions.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 250\",\"name\":\"Seminar in Mechanical Engineering\",\"description\":\"Weekly seminars on current mechanical engineering research presented by students, faculty, and invited experts. Repeatable for credit.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 255\",\"name\":\"Transport Processes in the Atmospheric Boundary Layer\",\"description\":\"Examines heat, mass, and momentum transport in the atmospheric boundary layer, including surface energy balance, similarity theory, and pollutant dispersion.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 261\",\"name\":\"Theory of Elasticity\",\"description\":\"Introduces tensor formulation, strain, equations of motion, constitutive relations, plane stress/strain problems, and variational principles in elasticity.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 266\",\"name\":\"Mechanics and Physics of Materials\",\"description\":\"Covers structure-property relationships, mechanical/thermal/electrical/magnetic behavior, phase transformations, and brittle-to-ductile transitions. Cross-listed with MSE 208.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 267\",\"name\":\"Finite Element Methods in Solid Mechanics\",\"description\":\"Presents Galerkin and energy methods for finite elements, static/dynamic analysis, multiphysics coupling, and automatic mesh generation.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 270\",\"name\":\"Introduction to Microelectromechanical Systems\",\"description\":\"Introduces MEMS design and fabrication, micromachining, material properties, transduction, sensors/actuators, microfluidics, packaging, reliability, and metrology. Cross-listed with MSE 238.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 271\",\"name\":\"Therapeutic Biomedical Microdevices\",\"description\":\"Covers microdevice fabrication for biomedical therapy, biocompatibility, and applications in cardiovascular, drug delivery, neuroprosthetic, and cellular engineering.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 272\",\"name\":\"Nanoscale Science and Engineering\",\"description\":\"Overviews nanometer-scale fabrication (lithography, self-assembly), and properties of nanoparticles, nanotubes, nanowires, biomolecules, and nanocomposites. Cross-listed with MSE 248.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 273\",\"name\":\"Principles and Designs of Micro Transducers\",\"description\":\"Explores physical principles and design of mechanical, thermal, electrical, magnetic, optical, chemical, and biological micro-scale sensors and actuators.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 274\",\"name\":\"Plasma-Aided Manufacturing and Materials Processing\",\"description\":\"Covers plasma physics, diagnostics, and use of plasmas for materials processing, including nanostructured material fabrication.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 278\",\"name\":\"Imperfections in Solids\",\"description\":\"Studies crystal defects, dislocation theory, stacking faults, twins, thin-film mechanics, and multilayer structures. Cross-listed with MSE 218.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 290\",\"name\":\"Directed Studies\",\"description\":\"Individual study of selected mechanical engineering topics under faculty supervision. Repeatable for credit.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 297\",\"name\":\"Directed Research\",\"description\":\"Faculty-supervised research on selected mechanical engineering problems. Repeatable for credit.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 298I\",\"name\":\"Individual Internship\",\"description\":\"Professional apprenticeship in mechanical engineering with academic oversight, including written work. Repeatable for credit.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 299\",\"name\":\"Research for the Thesis or Dissertation\",\"description\":\"Research toward the M.S. thesis or Ph.D. dissertation in mechanical engineering. Repeatable for credit.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"},\\n{\"course_id\":\"ME 302\",\"name\":\"Apprentice Teaching\",\"description\":\"Covers effective teaching methods, examination preparation/grading, and student interaction for TAs in mechanical engineering courses. Required each teaching quarter.\",\"level\":\"graduate\"}\\n]}',\n",
